 more tokens per megawatt than leading GPU systems. Company claim, not a benchmark. But when power is the constraint, the buyer with the biggest inference bill has every reason to build. Training likely stays","url":"https://x.com/Klaudnin3/status/2109644713737208245"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["13_2109740352491991041"]},"author_id":"1950884098056105986","created_at":"2026-10-12T20:18:10.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109740430896337256"],"entities":{"mentions":[{"end":22,"id":"20749410","start":16,"username":"finkd"}],"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/L740PaA04H","end":301,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/Joelc_eth/status/2109740430896337256/video/1","media_key":"13_2109740352491991041","start":278,"url":"https://t.co/L740PaA04H"}]},"id":"2109740430896337256","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":83,"like_count":2,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":1,"retweet_count":0},"text":"Mark Zuckerberg @finkd (Meta Founder and CEO) stated that operating a single one-gigawatt AI training cluster costs approximately $15 billion per year, while the upfront capital expenditure (CapEx) required to build it sits around $50 to $60 billion.\n\nAlexandr Wang, who joined https://t.co/L740PaA04H","url":"https://x.com/Joelc_eth/status/2109740430896337256"},{"attachments":{"media_keys":["3_2109639230804647936"]},"author_id":"343916123","created_at":"2026-10-12T13:37:37.000Z","edit_history_tweet_ids":["2109639629750116746"],"entities":{"urls":[{"display_url":"pic.x.com/cjLfb0Sjvi","end":301,"expanded_url":"https://x.com/shzhv13/status/2109639629750116746/photo/1","media_key":"3_2109639230804647936","start":278,"url":"https://t.co/cjLfb0Sjvi"}]},"id":"2109639629750116746","public_metrics":{"bookmark_count":0,"impression_count":236,"like_count":3,"quote_count":0,"reply_count":0,"retweet_count":3},"text":"Inference is now about two-thirds of AI compute. Most new capacity is still built like a training cluster.\n\nIn mining data centres, every machine worked on its own, so lo